<h2>Asobi 1.0 (build 1127) <span class="when">Oct 2, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Kitsu:</b> paste any Kitsu page link into Server (a playlist, a production) and Asobi connects to the server and picks that project and playlist for you, after Connect or Sign In.</li>
<li>Updates are much smaller: only what changed since your version is downloaded, usually about 1 MB instead of the whole app.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1117) <span class="when">Oct 1, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Export burn-ins use the web review's timecode format:</b> "f 0000 · 00:00:00:00" at top right.</li>
<li>Web reviews play straight through from one shot to the next with All clips on, instead of stopping at the start of each.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1115) <span class="when">Oct 1, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Delivery burn-ins for QuickTime exports:</b> choose shot name, timecode // frame, project or timeline name, date, and a custom line in the Export Movie save dialog. Shot name and timecode sit where the web review's burn-ins do. Your choices are remembered, and the session reel uses them too.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1112) <span class="when">Oct 1, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Joining a studio review over Tailscale is more reliable</b>, including when the host has just started the review again.</li>
<li>Web reviews show the playlist: a strip above the timeline with a block for each clip, and a preview when you hover it or the timeline.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1109) <span class="when">Oct 1, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Burn-ins on a running review:</b> turn the clip name and timecode on or off in the Share window's Options. It applies at once to clips you add, and Re-share applies it to the clips already shared.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1107) <span class="when">Oct 1, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Join studio reviews over Tailscale with the passphrase.</b> Join a Review now lists reviews hosted anywhere in the studio, marked "studio", not only ones on your own network.</li>
<li><b>Studio Reviews has Join</b> for any running review.</li>
<li>Clearer names in the Review Manager: Asobi Review License… and Asobi Seats….</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1104) <span class="when">Oct 1, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Choose how long a showcase lasts:</b> 1 month, 6 months, 12 months, or until you delete it. Web review links last 7 days, or longer if you choose.</li>
<li><b>Extend</b> a running review or showcase from the Review Manager. The links you've already sent keep working.</li>
<li><b>Who watched is kept for good</b>, even after a showcase ends, until you choose Delete Viewing Records… in the Review Manager.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1099) <span class="when">Oct 1, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>The studio watcher works away from the studio.</b> Reviews you host from home or on the road are registered with it too.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
